      {
        "Id": "c280c555cea640d8a808df8c5b36664d",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  open the floor plan with the shaft boxes.  Every box with an X (two lines corner to corner) in Revit lines (symbolic / detail / model) or in a CAD linked / imported in the plan becomes a SHAFT OPENING.  Height: base level + base offset, then top level + top offset, or blank top level = shaft height (6).  7 = the X drawn in every plan the shaft passes.  Run again with another height = the same shafts are updated (no doubles).",
        "DescriptionText": "",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
